betterquesting.quest.ld84AUxXU76p8RBdCeF90Q.name=§dAt the End of Science Lies Magic
betterquesting.quest.ld84AUxXU76p8RBdCeF90Q.desc=After building fusion and quantum machinery, you find yourself pouring magic into a fuel generator. The engineer calls it a second multiplier. The mage calls it overdue recognition.%n%nThe magic route offers larger base multipliers with a smaller permanent exponent. Base fluids are consumed; exponent cores are installed once. The two routes multiply together, and neither replaces the other.%n%nThe controller begins at exponent 1. Feed the next core tier into its lower-right slot to permanently raise that route. You cannot skip tiers, install a duplicate for another bonus, or use a Voltage Star in place of a core.%n%n[note]This is a reference branch. Survival recipes for base fluids, exponent cores, the controller and its light casing are not yet defined. Read and check the box; no pending material is requested or awarded, and this branch does not gate the fuel chain.[/note]
